  "term": "chaos theory",
  "definition": "Chaos theory is an approach to understanding dynamic systems by looking at how very small disturbances can cause their behavior to diverge over time. In this context, it provides the basis for measures of local dynamic stability that describe how sensitive movement patterns are to minor perturbations.",
